              - kind: RightParenthesis
                text: )
          - kind: Newline
            text: "\r\n"
          - kind: StatementList
            children:
              - kind: Newline
                text: "\r\n"
              - kind: EndOfLineComment
                text: "'This class always samples and compresses pictures in YCbCr colorspace.  The first component, Y,"
              - kind: Newline
                text: "\r\n"
              - kind: EndOfLineComment
                text: "'represents the Luminance of the pixels.  This is \"how bright\" a pixel is.  The Cb and Cr"
              - kind: Newline
                text: "\r\n"
              - kind: EndOfLineComment
                text: "'components are Chrominance, which is a measure of how far from neutral-white (toward a color)"
              - kind: Newline
                text: "\r\n"
              - kind: EndOfLineComment
                text: "'a pixel is.  The human visual sensory system can discriminate Luminance differences about"
              - kind: Newline
                text: "\r\n"
              - kind: EndOfLineComment
                text: "'twice as well as it can discriminate Chrominance differences."
              - kind: Newline
                text: "\r\n"
              - kind: EndOfLineComment
                text: "'"
              - kind: Newline
                text: "\r\n"
              - kind: EndOfLineComment
                text: "'Virtually all JPEG files are in YCbCr colorspace.  Other JPEG compliant colorspaces exist, but"
              - kind: Newline
                text: "\r\n"
              - kind: EndOfLineComment
                text: "'they are used in specialty equipment.  For example, people in the astronomy or medical fields"
              - kind: Newline
                text: "\r\n"
              - kind: EndOfLineComment
                text: "'choose colorspaces that best record the information they are interested in, and don't care about"
              - kind: Newline
                text: "\r\n"
              - kind: EndOfLineComment
                text: "'how pretty the picture looks to a person when displayed on a computer monitor."
              - kind: Newline
                text: "\r\n"
              - kind: EndOfLineComment
                text: "'[Apple/Machintosh sometimes uses a four component colorspace, but that colorspace is rare and"
              - kind: Newline
                text: "\r\n"
              - kind: EndOfLineComment
                text: "'not widely supported]"
              - kind: Newline
                text: "\r\n"
              - kind: EndOfLineComment
                text: "'"
              - kind: Newline
                text: "\r\n"
              - kind: EndOfLineComment
                text: "'Sampling frequencies define how often each component is sampled.  Higher frequencies store more"
              - kind: Newline
                text: "\r\n"
              - kind: EndOfLineComment
                text: "'information, while lower frequencies store less.  Typically, sampling frequencies are set at"
              - kind: Newline
                text: "\r\n"
              - kind: EndOfLineComment
                text: "'2,2, 1,1, 1,1.  This corresponds to the human visual sensory system.  The first component,"
              - kind: Newline
                text: "\r\n"
              - kind: EndOfLineComment
                text: "'Luminance, is sampled twice as much because our eyes notice differences in Luminance quite easily."
              - kind: Newline
                text: "\r\n"
              - kind: EndOfLineComment
                text: "'The two Chrominance components are sampled half as much as because our eyes can't distinguish"
              - kind: Newline
                text: "\r\n"
              - kind: EndOfLineComment
                text: "'the difference in color changes as well.  One Luminance value is sampled for every pixel, and"
              - kind: Newline
                text: "\r\n"
              - kind: EndOfLineComment
                text: "'one Chrominance value is sampled for each 2X2 block of pixels."
              - kind: Newline
                text: "\r\n"
              - kind: EndOfLineComment
                text: "'"
              - kind: Newline
                text: "\r\n"
              - kind: EndOfLineComment
                text: "'Digital cameras typically record at sampling frequencies of 1,1, 1,1, 1,1.  This samples every"
              - kind: Newline
                text: "\r\n"
              - kind: EndOfLineComment
                text: "'pixel for all three components.  The quality of the picture is a little better when viewed by"
              - kind: Newline
                text: "\r\n"
              - kind: EndOfLineComment
                text: "'a person, but the compression benefits drop significantly.  If the picture to be compressed"
              - kind: Newline
                text: "\r\n"
              - kind: EndOfLineComment
                text: "'is from a Scanner or Digital camera, and you plan on printing it in the future, and storage"
              - kind: Newline
                text: "\r\n"
              - kind: EndOfLineComment
                text: "'space is not a problem, then sampling at these frequencies makes sense.  Otherwise, if you only"
              - kind: Newline
                text: "\r\n"
              - kind: EndOfLineComment
                text: "'plan on using the picture to display on a monitor or a web page, [2,2, 1,1, 1,1] makes the"
              - kind: Newline
                text: "\r\n"
              - kind: EndOfLineComment
                text: "'most sense."
              - kind: Newline
                text: "\r\n"
              - kind: EndOfLineComment
                text: "'"
              - kind: Newline
                text: "\r\n"
              - kind: EndOfLineComment
                text: "'The JPEG standard specifies that sampling frequencies may range from 1-4 for each component"
              - kind: Newline
                text: "\r\n"
              - kind: EndOfLineComment
                text: "'in both directions.  However, if any component has a sampling frequency of '3', and another"
              - kind: Newline
                text: "\r\n"
              - kind: EndOfLineComment
                text: "'component has a coresponding sampling frequency of '2' or '4', the downsampling process"
              - kind: Newline
                text: "\r\n"
              - kind: EndOfLineComment
                text: "'will map fractional pixels to sample values.  This is leagal in the JPEG standard, and this"
              - kind: Newline
                text: "\r\n"
              - kind: EndOfLineComment
                text: "'class will compress fractional pixel samplings, but this is not widely supported.  It is"
              - kind: Newline
                text: "\r\n"
              - kind: EndOfLineComment
                text: "'highly recommended to AVOID SAMPLING FACTORS OF 3 for maximum compatability with JPEG decoders."
              - kind: Newline
                text: "\r\n"
              - kind: EndOfLineComment
                text: "'"
              - kind: Newline
                text: "\r\n"
              - kind: EndOfLineComment
                text: "'Some JPEG encoders avoid the fractional pixel problem by only allowing the end user to pick"
              - kind: Newline
                text: "\r\n"
              - kind: EndOfLineComment
                text: "'a \"sub-sampling\" value.  In such \"Sub Sampling\" schemes, all Chrominance frequencies are set"
              - kind: Newline
                text: "\r\n"
              - kind: EndOfLineComment
                text: "'to one, and the (one or two) sub-sampling value(s) specify Luminance frequencies."
              - kind: Newline
                text: "\r\n"
              - kind: EndOfLineComment
                text: "'"
              - kind: Newline
                text: "\r\n"
              - kind: EndOfLineComment
                text: "'There should *never* be an error raised if you are using this class correctly.  It should"
              - kind: Newline
                text: "\r\n"
              - kind: EndOfLineComment
                text: "'not be possible for the end user to specify illegal sampling frequency values!"
              - kind: Newline
                text: "\r\n"
              - kind: EndOfLineComment
                text: "'[For tinkerers - If you delete the error raising code and specify illegal sampling"
              - kind: Newline
                text: "\r\n"
              - kind: EndOfLineComment
                text: "'frequencies, this class will procede to create a non-JPEG compliant file with the values"
              - kind: Newline
                text: "\r\n"
              - kind: EndOfLineComment
                text: "'specified]"
              - kind: Newline
                text: "\r\n"
              - kind: Newline
                text: "\r\n"
